id: ops-evidence-expiry
title: Invalidate only operational claims whose evidence expires or whose scoped versions change
description: "Acceptance: attach explicit freshness and scope requirements to accepted health, coverage and recovery receipts. Changing a relevant package or backend version invalidates only affected claims. Unavailable evidence never becomes a pass. Deliver typed SDK, agent-sized TOON/JSON CLI, refusals with remedies, docs, non-git real-tracker validation and npm/Bun CI release gates."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-22T16:06:35.472Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T16:19:52.602Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-22T16:06:40.798Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check: pinned core SDK assurance owns declarations, scope validation, assertion evaluation and verified durable verdict history (listAssuranceVerdicts); pm-review/src/round.ts gates exact PR heads and completed checks. pm-context receipts track context usage. pm-ops assurance.ts refuses source-stale lcov and backend-capabilities.ts audits list/get/schema contracts. None evaluates retained operational health/coverage/recovery evidence against cross-package and backend version scopes plus wall-clock freshness. Plan: bind explicit policies to core immutable assertion receipts and use the SDK verified verdict reader; no parallel assurance store, contract evaluator, Git dependency or tracker mutation on evaluation. Published CLI latest verified as 2026.10.22; preserve the repo SDK pin 2026.10.17."
  "2026-10-22T16:14:29.378Z",codex-agent,"Implementation: exact core gate/tree/time/assertion attachment, core population scope, exclusive TTL boundary and explicit relevant identity map. Directory audit uses listAssuranceVerdicts, readHistorySnapshot and verifyHistoryRecordHash; core scope semantics are reused with an additional boundary guard because the pinned assertion validator accepts an unknown scope kind. Read-only non-git tests compare every tracker byte and remove Git from PATH. Targeted expiry and renderer suites pass 16/16. Default diagnostic output bounds rows and preserves full counts; ok is the authoritative diagnostic predicate, consistent with ops capabilities. No hosted access or dependency bump."
  "2026-10-22T16:18:19.441Z",codex-agent,"Real-data validation: read-only non-git export of public main 3546c385e30d9914ab8a5690ccee7842ca38a7d9 contained 148 items, 6 types, 309 files and zero core gate verdicts; SDK warnings 0. Three claims stayed unavailable (evidence_missing) before and after changing all scoped versions; 0 fresh, 0 revalidate, 3 unavailable. Compact JSON 882 bytes. All tracker bytes unchanged. Positive controls use separate real initialized scratch trackers with SDK-evaluated sealed verdicts. Focused expiry coverage is 100/100/100/100. Behavioral revert proofs: bypassing version invalidation fails selective regression (0 pass/1 fail); bypassing hash refusal fails tamper regression (0 pass/1 fail); source restored. SDK listAssuranceVerdicts reads durable receipts; separate SDK hash checks establish record integrity, not global authentication."
  "2026-10-22T16:19:52.602Z",codex-agent,"Local acceptance: 18/18 targeted expiry and renderer regressions pass, including actual installed CLI TOON/JSON parsing, typed invalid-option exit 2 and no Git executable. Typecheck, test typecheck, build, lint, zero-duplication and docstring checks pass at unchanged thresholds. Focused expiry module coverage is four 100 percent dimensions. Full npm and Bun release gates will run in CI because the shared host is saturated. Boundary notes: consumers must include every relevant version identity; pure remote evaluation trusts authenticated caller receipts; history search is bounded to newest 1000 verdicts. No operational health/coverage/recovery certification is claimed from missing public receipts."
